# Tell GitHub's Linguist that the notebooks are documentation, not source.
#
# Why: notebooks are byte-heavy because each rendered output (matplotlib
# figures, training-log text dumps, prediction overlays) is embedded as
# base64 inside the .ipynb JSON. Counted by raw bytes, our 5 notebooks
# (~31 MB total) drown out the Python sources (~400 KB) and make GitHub's
# language bar show 98% "Jupyter Notebook" -- not representative of the
# actual codebase. `linguist-documentation` excludes them from the language
# stats while keeping them in the repo and still rendered inline by GitHub.
notebooks/*.ipynb linguist-documentation
